1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,629
Welcome to Melody and
Barnaby's Music Nuggets!

2
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:09,877
Today we are going to find Middle C.

3
00:00:11,877 --> 00:00:15,985
Here is a keyboard…
and here is the stave.

4
00:00:16,585 --> 00:00:21,250
They show the same notes…
in two different ways.

5
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:27,769
Look at the middle of the keyboard.

6
00:00:28,369 --> 00:00:33,499
Just to the left of the
two black keys… is C.

7
00:00:36,699 --> 00:00:44,429
This is the C nearest the middle of
the piano… so it is called Middle C.

8
00:00:48,229 --> 00:00:51,269
Now find it on the stave.

9
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:58,631
Middle C sits on a little line of
its own… just below the treble stave.

10
00:01:00,431 --> 00:01:06,722
You can also write it just above the
bass stave… It is the very same note.

11
00:01:09,322 --> 00:01:16,774
Two ways to write it… but only one
Middle C… in the middle of the keyboard.

12
00:01:20,174 --> 00:01:26,464
Up here is the treble clef… for
the right hand… and higher notes.

13
00:01:28,864 --> 00:01:35,295
Down here is the bass clef… for
the left hand… and lower notes.

14
00:01:37,695 --> 00:01:40,595
Middle C is where the hands meet.

15
00:01:44,395 --> 00:01:46,181
Let's play Middle C.

16
00:01:52,381 --> 00:01:55,375
Your turn! Look at the notes.

17
00:01:55,875 --> 00:01:59,286
Where is Middle C on the keyboard?

18
00:02:03,586 --> 00:02:04,786
Here.

19
00:02:06,569 --> 00:02:09,794
Which hand plays the bass clef?

20
00:02:13,894 --> 00:02:15,634
The left hand.

21
00:02:17,434 --> 00:02:19,870
Is this note Middle C?

22
00:02:23,970 --> 00:02:25,170
Yes!

23
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,142
You've got it!

24
00:02:28,842 --> 00:02:30,303
Now it's your turn!

25
00:02:30,403 --> 00:02:34,140
Play the note ladder
and find Middle C!

26
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,629
See you for the next Nugget!

